# NIST time sources for the wall.
#
# A drop-in, not a replacement for /etc/chrony/chrony.conf -- that file belongs
# to the chrony package, and the repo's copy of it was the stock Ubuntu one with
# these four lines swapped in. Shipping the whole file would clobber a conffile
# that is not ours to own; the stock file already reads this directory.
#
# These are load-bearing, not a preference: calendar-kiosk refuses to start
# Chromium until chrony reports Leap status Normal and the system clock within
# 10ms of its reference. A wall whose clock is wrong shows the wrong day.
server time-a-b.nist.gov iburst
server time-b-b.nist.gov iburst
server time-a-wwv.nist.gov iburst
server time-b-wwv.nist.gov iburst
